 "text": "Skip to Main Content\n\ninfo@mazingirasafari.com\n\n+255784278205\n\nAbout Us\nContact\nFAQ's\nYour Trip\nTravel Info\nBlog\nVisa's & Entry Requirements,\nVisa and Entry Requirements for Tanzania\n​\n\n1. Visa Requirements:\n\nGeneral Requirement: Most travelers require a visa to enter Tanzania. Visitors should check specific requirements based on their country of origin.\n\nTypes of Visas:\n\nTourist Visa: Generally valid for 90 days for tourists visiting for leisure.\n\nBusiness Visa: For short-term business, meetings, or conferences.\n\nTransit Visa: For travelers passing through Tanzania en route to another destination.\n\nVisa Application:\n\nE-Visa: Travelers can apply for an e-visa via the official Tanzania Immigration website, which is recommended to simplify the entry process.\n\nVisa on Arrival: Available at major entry points like Julius Nyerere International Airport (Dar es Salaam), Kilimanjaro International Airport, and Zanzibar International Airport. Obtaining an e-visa in advance is advisable to avoid delays.\n\nEmbassy Visa: Can be obtained at Tanzanian embassies or consulates in the home country.\n\n​\n\n​\n\n​\n\n2. Entry Requirements:\n\nPassport Validity: Passports must be valid for at least six months after the date of entry.\n\nReturn Ticket: Proof of a return ticket or onward journey may be required.\n\nVaccination:\n\nYellow Fever: A vaccination certificate is necessary if coming from or transiting through a country with risk of Yellow Fever.\n\nCOVID-19: Check the latest health guidelines for any COVID-19 related entry requirements.\n\nFinancial Proof: Evidence of sufficient funds to cover the stay may be requested.\n\n​\n\n3. Health Precautions:\n\nMalaria Prevention: Malaria is prevalent in Tanzania. It is highly recommended to take malaria prophylaxis. Consult with a healthcare professional to discuss appropriate malaria medication and other travel health advice well before your trip.\n\nHealth Insurance: Travel health insurance is recommended to cover any medical expenses.\n\n​\n\n4. Special Considerations:\n\nZanzibar: Note that Zanzibar operates under different local regulations and may have additional entry requirements.\n\n​\n\n5. Additional Tips:\n\nStay Informed: Visa policies and entry requirements can change. Regularly check updates from the Tanzania Immigration Service or consult the nearest Tanzanian embassy or consulate before traveling.\n\n​\n\nThese guidelines offer a comprehensive overview, but travelers should ensure they check the latest information and consult health professionals for specific travel health advice.\n\nOFFICIAL VISA APPLICATIONS\nWidget Didn’t Load\nCheck your internet and refresh this page.\nIf that doesn’t work, contact us.\nRefresh this page\nContact us\n\ninfo@mazingirasafari.com\n\nuk.sales@mazingirasafari.com\n\n+255784278205 / +255767278204\n\nAccessibility Statement \n\nMazingira Eco Friendly Safari Adventure\n\nArusha \n\nP.O Box 12544\n\nStay informed, join our newsletter\n\nEnter your email here \nSubscribe\n\nMazingira Safari © 2023 | ",
